 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why did Frederic Tudor ship a frozen lake to the tropics?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 2.924
  },
  {
   "text": "His ship sails into Caribbean heat, packed with 130 tons of ice.",
   "s": 3.224,
   "e": 7.174
  },
  {
   "text": "If it melts, he loses every penny he owns.",
   "s": 7.374,
   "e": 9.367
  },
  {
   "text": "Back in Boston, everyone laughed. Newspapers called it a slippery idea.",
   "s": 9.567,
   "e": 13.357
  },
  {
   "text": "Then he lands, and the ice is already dripping off the dock.",
   "s": 13.558,
   "e": 16.185
  },
  {
   "text": "Worse, nobody on the island has ever seen ice before.",
   "s": 16.385,
   "e": 19.047
  },
  {
   "text": "They poke it. They sniff it. One brave man licks it. Then they all watch it melt.",
   "s": 19.247,
   "e": 22.972
  },
  {
   "text": "So Tudor loses all his money, and his fortune turns into puddles!",
   "s": 23.172,
   "e": 26.305
  },
  {
   "text": "But he sails home, and tries again. And again.",
   "s": 26.505,
   "e": 28.629
  },
  {
   "text": "His ice keeps melting, and the laughing gets louder.",
   "s": 28.829,
   "e": 31.207
  },
  {
   "text": "Some days, he can't even pay for his own lunch.",
   "s": 31.407,
   "e": 33.526
  },
  {
   "text": "So how do you sell ice to people who don't even want it?",
   "s": 33.726,
   "e": 36.106
  },
  {
   "text": "Two tricks. First, he packs every block in sawdust, like a cozy blanket.",
   "s": 36.406,
   "e": 40.054
  },
  {
   "text": "Second, he gives bartenders free ice, so every drink comes ice cold.",
   "s": 40.254,
   "e": 43.913
  },
  {
   "text": "One cold sip, and nobody wants a warm drink ever again.",
   "s": 44.313,
   "e": 47.283
  },
  {
   "text": "Soon his ice sails to Cuba, to Brazil, even to India, four months at sea.",
   "s": 47.483,
   "e": 51.533
  },
  {
   "text": "Ice cream, cold lemonade, a clinking glass in every hand.",
   "s": 51.733,
   "e": 54.622
  },
  {
   "text": "The man everyone laughed at becomes the Ice King.",
   "s": 54.822,
   "e": 57.031
  },
  {
   "text": "And that's why a frozen lake went to the tropics.",
   "s": 57.231,
   "e": 59.36
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow for a weird story every day. Like this one:",
   "s": 59.56,
   "e": 62.147
  }
 ],
